<Docs title="Usage" description="Day-to-day puck commands.">
  <h1>Usage</h1>
  <pre><code>puck doctor                  # blockers before switching
puck install                 # install from composer.lock
puck install --no-dev        # production install
puck install --offline       # warm store only; no network
puck dump-autoload -o        # regenerate optimized autoload
puck require vendor/package
puck remove vendor/package
puck update                  # refresh lock + install
puck upgrade                 # self-update from GitHub Releases
puck store path              # print the global store path
puck store gc                # garbage-collect unused store entries</code></pre>

  <h2>Timings</h2>
  <p>
    Set <code>PUCK_TIMINGS=1</code> to print phase timings on stderr
    (<code>plan_ms</code>, <code>download_ms</code>, <code>extract_ms</code>,{' '}
    <code>overlap_ms</code>, <code>link_ms</code>, <code>dump_ms</code>, ...).
    <code>download_ms</code> is a sum across concurrent fetches;
    <code>overlap_ms</code> is <code>(download_ms + extract_ms) − wall</code> (mostly HTTP concurrency).
  </p>

  <h2>What stays the same</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>composer.json</code> / <code>composer.lock</code>: same format Composer reads</li>
    <li>
      <code>vendor/</code>: real directory (hardlink / reflink / copy from the store). Shared
      inodes mean edits under <code>vendor/</code> can change the store — do not hand-edit.
    </li>
    <li>You can run Composer again on the same project after puck</li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
